module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Injective
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LocalizedModule.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Spectrum.Prime.Noetherian
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Support
public import Mathlib.Topology.NoetherianSpace

/-!
# Spreading out the vanishing of a map of finite modules, and making it uniform

The uniformity paragraph in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0EFX] turns a bound depending on a prime
`𝔮` into a bound that works for every prime of the set `T` at once. Stripped of the local
duality that feeds it, that paragraph is three mechanisms, and this module proves them.

*Spreading out.* A map `h : M → N` of modules over a Noetherian ring whose localization at `𝔮`
vanishes already vanishes after localizing at every prime of an open neighbourhood of `𝔮`,
provided `N` is finite: the primes at which the localization of `h` vanishes are exactly the
primes outside the support of the image of `h`, the image is again a finite module, and the
support of a finite module is the closed set cut out by its annihilator. This is
`isOpen_setOf_forall_exists_smul_eq_zero`, with
`isLocalizedModule_map_eq_zero_iff` identifying the elementwise condition that appears in it
with the vanishing of the localized map in any model of the localization. The same argument on
the cokernel spreads out the **surjectivity** of a localized map of finite modules,
`isOpen_setOf_forall_exists_smul_mem_range`: that is the second shrinking of the neighbourhood
`W` in the source's proof, where what is spread out is the surjectivity of
`E(0, -d-s-1) → E(m, -d-s-1)/K_{m'}`.

*Uniformity.* If a monotone family of open sets `V d n` covers each level set of a function `δ`
with finite image on `T`, then one index `N` works at every point of `T`:
`exists_forall_mem_of_finite_image_of_monotone`. The spectrum of a Noetherian ring is a
Noetherian topological space, in which *every* subset is quasi-compact, so no separate
hypothesis on `T` is needed; the finitely many level sets are the sets `T_d` of the source, and
`δ` is the dimension function of a dualizing complex, whose image is finite by
`Stacks.Algebraization.finite_range_dimensionFunction`.

*Detection.* Over a local ring, a map of modules is zero as soon as every map of its target into
an injective module with a nonzero socle element kills it, and — this is the form the reverse
direction of the source's local duality step needs — it is already zero when the maps that kill
it merely span the dual modulo the maximal ideal, provided the target is `𝔪`-power torsion:
`eq_zero_of_forall_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero`. This is the step that reads the vanishing of a
Matlis dual back as the vanishing of a map, and it needs only one nonzero element of the target
annihilated by the maximal ideal — the socle of an injective hull of the residue field provides
one. No completeness and no biduality enter: the module generated by a nonzero element of the
source's image is a quotient of the ring by a proper ideal, and the socle element defines a map
out of that quotient which the injectivity of the ambient module extends.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isLocalizedModule_map_eq_zero_iff` — the localization of a map
  vanishes exactly when every value of the map is annihilated by an element of the multiplicative
  set.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isOpen_setOf_forall_exists_smul_eq_zero` — the locus of primes at which
  the localization of a map into a finite module vanishes is open.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isLocalizedModule_map_surjective_iff` — the localization of a map is
  surjective exactly when every element of the target is carried into the image by an element of
  the multiplicative set.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.notMem_support_quotient_range_iff`,
  `Stacks.LocalCohomology.isOpen_setOf_forall_exists_smul_mem_range` — the locus of primes at
  which a map of finite modules localizes to a **surjection** is open, that locus being the
  complement of the support of the cokernel.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_forall_mem_of_finite_image_of_monotone` — one index serves the
  whole of `T` when the level sets of `δ` on `T` are finitely many and each is covered by a
  monotone family of opens.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.eq_zero_of_forall_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero` — a map over a local
  ring is detected by the maps of its target into an injective module with a nonzero socle
  element.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_mem_span_ne_zero_maximalIdeal_smul_eq_zero` — a nonzero element
  of a module killed by a power of the maximal ideal spans a submodule containing a nonzero
  element killed by the maximal ideal itself.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.eq_zero_of_forall_mem_comp_eq_zero_of_sup_eq_top` — the sharpening of
  the detection step that the **reverse** direction of the local duality transport of
  [Stacks, Tag 0EFX] needs: it is enough that the maps killing the given map span the dual
  *modulo the maximal ideal*, provided the target is killed elementwise by a power of the maximal
  ideal.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EFX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EFX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00L2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00L2), the support of a finite
  module.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

/-! ### The vanishing of a localized map -/

/-- **The localization of a map, read elementwise.** For any model `f` of the localization of
`M` and `g` of the localization of `N` at a multiplicative set `S`, the localized map of
`h : M → N` vanishes exactly when every value of `h` is annihilated by an element of `S`. -/
theorem isLocalizedModule_map_eq_zero_iff {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (S : Submonoid A)
    {M M' N N' : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup M'] [Module A M']
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [AddCommGroup N'] [Module A N']
    (f : M →ₗ[A] M') [IsLocalizedModule S f] (g : N →ₗ[A] N') [IsLocalizedModule S g]
    (h : M →ₗ[A] N) :
    IsLocalizedModule.map S f g h = 0 ↔ ∀ m : M, ∃ r ∈ S, r • h m = 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro hmap m
    have hzero : g (h m) = 0 := by
      rw [← IsLocalizedModule.map_apply S f g h m, hmap]
      rfl
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff S g).mp hzero
    exact ⟨r.1, r.2, hr⟩
  · intro hm
    refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
    obtain ⟨⟨m, s⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.mk'_surjective S f x
    obtain ⟨r, hrS, hr⟩ := hm m
    rw [Function.uncurry_apply_pair, IsLocalizedModule.map_mk' S f g h m s]
    exact (IsLocalizedModule.mk'_eq_zero' g s).mpr ⟨⟨r, hrS⟩, hr⟩

/-- A prime lies outside the support of the image of a map exactly when every value of the map
is annihilated by an element not in the prime. -/
theorem notMem_support_range_iff {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    {M N : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    (h : M →ₗ[A] N) (p : PrimeSpectrum A) :
    p ∉ Module.support A ↥(LinearMap.range h) ↔ ∀ m : M, ∃ r ∉ p.asIdeal, r • h m = 0 := by
  rw [Module.notMem_support_iff']
  constructor
  · intro hx m
    obtain ⟨r, hr, hrm⟩ := hx ⟨h m, ⟨m, rfl⟩⟩
    exact ⟨r, hr, congrArg Subtype.val hrm⟩
  · rintro hm ⟨-, m, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨r, hr, hrm⟩ := hm m
    exact ⟨r, hr, Subtype.ext hrm⟩

/-- **Spreading out the vanishing of a localized map.** Over a Noetherian ring, for a map `h`
into a finite module the set of primes at which the localization of `h` vanishes is open.

The set is the complement of the support of the image of `h`, which is a finite module because
a submodule of a finite module over a Noetherian ring is finite, and the support of a finite
module is the zero locus of its annihilator. -/
theorem isOpen_setOf_forall_exists_smul_eq_zero {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {M N : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    [Module.Finite A N] (h : M →ₗ[A] N) :
    IsOpen {p : PrimeSpectrum A | ∀ m : M, ∃ r ∉ p.asIdeal, r • h m = 0} := by
  have : IsNoetherian A N := isNoetherian_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite A N
  have hfin : Module.Finite A ↥(LinearMap.range h) :=
    Module.Finite.iff_fg.mpr (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  have hset : {p : PrimeSpectrum A | ∀ m : M, ∃ r ∉ p.asIdeal, r • h m = 0} =
      (Module.support A ↥(LinearMap.range h))ᶜ :=
    Set.ext fun p => (notMem_support_range_iff h p).symm
  rw [hset, Module.support_eq_zeroLocus]
  exact (PrimeSpectrum.isClosed_zeroLocus _).isOpen_compl

/-! ### The locus where a map of finite modules localizes to a surjection -/

/-- **The surjectivity of a localized map, read elementwise.** For any model `f` of the
localization of `M` and `g` of the localization of `N` at a multiplicative set `S`, the localized
map of `h : M → N` is surjective exactly when every element of `N` is carried into the image of
`h` by an element of `S`.

This is the surjectivity counterpart of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.isLocalizedModule_map_eq_zero_iff`, and like it the criterion mentions
no model, so a surjectivity statement proved in one model holds in every other. -/
theorem isLocalizedModule_map_surjective_iff {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (S : Submonoid A)
    {M M' N N' : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup M'] [Module A M']
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [AddCommGroup N'] [Module A N']
    (f : M →ₗ[A] M') [IsLocalizedModule S f] (g : N →ₗ[A] N') [IsLocalizedModule S g]
    (h : M →ₗ[A] N) :
    Function.Surjective (IsLocalizedModule.map S f g h) ↔
      ∀ n : N, ∃ r ∈ S, r • n ∈ LinearMap.range h := by
  constructor
  · intro hsurj n
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hsurj (g n)
    obtain ⟨⟨m, s⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.mk'_surjective S f x
    rw [Function.uncurry_apply_pair, IsLocalizedModule.map_mk' S f g h m s] at hx
    have hx' : IsLocalizedModule.mk' g n 1 = IsLocalizedModule.mk' g (h m) s :=
      (IsLocalizedModule.mk'_one (S := S) g n).trans hx.symm
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (IsLocalizedModule.mk'_eq_mk'_iff g n (h m) 1 s).1 hx'
    refine ⟨(c : A) * (s : A), mul_mem c.2 s.2, (c : A) • m, ?_⟩
    rw [map_smul, mul_smul]
    simpa [Submonoid.smul_def] using hc
  · intro hmem y
    obtain ⟨⟨n, t⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.mk'_surjective S g y
    obtain ⟨r, hrS, m, hm⟩ := hmem n
    refine ⟨IsLocalizedModule.mk' f m (⟨r, hrS⟩ * t), ?_⟩
    rw [Function.uncurry_apply_pair,
      IsLocalizedModule.map_mk' S f g h m (⟨r, hrS⟩ * t), hm]
    exact IsLocalizedModule.mk'_cancel_left g n ⟨r, hrS⟩ t

/-- A prime lies outside the support of the cokernel of a map exactly when every element of the
target is carried into the image by an element outside the prime. -/
theorem notMem_support_quotient_range_iff {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    {M N : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    (h : M →ₗ[A] N) (p : PrimeSpectrum A) :
    p ∉ Module.support A (N ⧸ LinearMap.range h) ↔
      ∀ n : N, ∃ r ∉ p.asIdeal, r • n ∈ LinearMap.range h := by
  rw [Module.notMem_support_iff']
  constructor
  · intro hx n
    obtain ⟨r, hr, hrn⟩ := hx (Submodule.Quotient.mk n)
    refine ⟨r, hr, ?_⟩
    rwa [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at hrn
  · intro hn x
    obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
    obtain ⟨r, hr, hrn⟩ := hn n
    exact ⟨r, hr, by rwa [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]⟩

/-- **Spreading out the surjectivity of a localized map.** Over a Noetherian ring, for a map `h`
of finite modules the set of primes at which the localization of `h` is a surjection is open.

The set is the complement of the support of the cokernel of `h`, which is a finite module as a
quotient of one, and the support of a finite module is the closed set cut out by its
annihilator. This is the second shrinking of the neighbourhood `W` in the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0EFX], where the map whose surjectivity is spread out is
`E(0, -d-s-1) → E(m, -d-s-1)/K_{m'}`. -/
theorem isOpen_setOf_forall_exists_smul_mem_range {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    {M N : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    [Module.Finite A N] (h : M →ₗ[A] N) :
    IsOpen {p : PrimeSpectrum A | ∀ n : N, ∃ r ∉ p.asIdeal, r • n ∈ LinearMap.range h} := by
  have hset : {p : PrimeSpectrum A | ∀ n : N, ∃ r ∉ p.asIdeal, r • n ∈ LinearMap.range h} =
      (Module.support A (N ⧸ LinearMap.range h))ᶜ :=
    Set.ext fun p => (notMem_support_quotient_range_iff h p).symm
  rw [hset, Module.support_eq_zeroLocus]
  exact (PrimeSpectrum.isClosed_zeroLocus _).isOpen_compl

/-! ### Making a bound uniform over the level sets of a function with finite image -/

/-- **One index for the whole of `T`.** Let `X` be a Noetherian topological space, `T ⊆ X` and
`δ : X → ℤ` a function taking finitely many values on `T`. If for every `d` the level set
`T ∩ δ⁻¹(d)` is covered by a monotone family of open sets `V d n`, then there is a single index
`N` with `x ∈ V (δ x) N` for every `x ∈ T`.

Every subset of a Noetherian space is quasi-compact, so each level set is covered by finitely
many members of its family and hence, by monotonicity, by a single one; the finitely many
resulting indices have a maximum. -/
theorem exists_forall_mem_of_finite_image_of_monotone {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]
    [TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace X] (T : Set X) (δ : X → ℤ) (hδ : (δ '' T).Finite)
    (V : ℤ → ℕ → Set X) (hopen : ∀ d n, IsOpen (V d n)) (hmono : ∀ d, Monotone (V d))
    (hcov : ∀ d : ℤ, T ∩ δ ⁻¹' {d} ⊆ ⋃ n, V d n) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ x ∈ T, x ∈ V (δ x) N := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ d : ℤ, ∃ n : ℕ, T ∩ δ ⁻¹' {d} ⊆ V d n := by
    intro d
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace.isCompact
      (T ∩ δ ⁻¹' {d})).elim_finite_subcover (V d) (hopen d) (hcov d)
    refine ⟨s.sup id, fun x hx => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨n, hn, hxn⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hs hx)
    exact hmono d (Finset.le_sup (f := id) hn) hxn
  choose Nd hNd using key
  refine ⟨hδ.toFinset.sup Nd, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  exact hmono (δ x) (Finset.le_sup (f := Nd) (hδ.mem_toFinset.mpr ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩))
    (hNd (δ x) ⟨hx, rfl⟩)

/-! ### Detecting a map by the maps of its target into an injective module -/

/-- **A map over a local ring is detected by the maps into an injective module with a nonzero
socle element.** Let `R` be a local ring, let `E` be an injective `R`-module and let `e ∈ E` be
a nonzero element annihilated by the maximal ideal. If every `R`-linear map `H' → E` kills
`φ : H → H'`, then `φ = 0`.

*Argument.* If `φ x ≠ 0`, write `y = φ x`. The annihilator `K` of `y` is a proper ideal, hence
contained in the maximal ideal, so `r ↦ r • e` kills `K` and descends to a map `R ⧸ K → E`
sending the class of `1` to `e`. The map `R ⧸ K → H'` sending the class of `r` to `r • y` is
injective, so injectivity of `E` extends the first map to `ψ : H' → E` with `ψ y = e ≠ 0`,
contradicting `ψ ∘ φ = 0`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_forall_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {E : Type u} [AddCommGroup E] [Module R E] [Module.Injective R E]
    (e : E) (he : e ≠ 0) (hme : ∀ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R, a • e = 0)
    {H H' : Type u} [AddCommGroup H] [Module R H] [AddCommGroup H'] [Module R H']
    (φ : H →ₗ[R] H') (hφ : ∀ ψ : H' →ₗ[R] E, ψ ∘ₗ φ = 0) : φ = 0 := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.zero_apply]
  by_contra hx
  have hKne : LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x)) ≠ ⊤ := by
    intro htop
    refine hx ?_
    have h1 : (1 : R) ∈ LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x)) :=
      htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top
    rwa [LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply_one] at h1
  have hKe : LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x)) ≤
      LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R E e) := by
    intro r hr
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply]
    exact hme r (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hKne hr)
  have hι₀inj : Function.Injective
      ((LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x))).liftQ
        (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x)) le_rfl) := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot]
    exact Submodule.ker_liftQ_eq_bot' _ _ rfl
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ⟩ := Module.Injective.out (R := R) (Q := E) _ hι₀inj
    ((LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x))).liftQ
      (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R E e) hKe)
  have hψy : ψ (φ x) = e := by
    have h1 := hψ ((LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' (φ x))).mkQ 1)
    rwa [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.liftQ_apply, Submodule.liftQ_apply,
      LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply_one, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply_one] at h1
  exact he (hψy.symm.trans (LinearMap.congr_fun (hφ ψ) x))

/-! ### Detection through a submodule of the dual that is dense modulo the maximal ideal -/

/-- **A nonzero element killed by a power of the maximal ideal spans a submodule with a nonzero
socle element.** If `x ≠ 0` and `𝔪ⁿ` kills `x`, then `R · x` contains a nonzero element killed
by `𝔪`.

Induction on `n`. For `n = 0` the hypothesis gives `x = 1 • x = 0`. For `n + 1`, either some
`a ∈ 𝔪ⁿ` has `a • x ≠ 0`, and then `a • x` is killed by `𝔪` because `𝔪 · 𝔪ⁿ = 𝔪^{n+1}` kills
`x`; or every `a ∈ 𝔪ⁿ` kills `x`, and the induction hypothesis applies. -/
theorem exists_mem_span_ne_zero_maximalIdeal_smul_eq_zero {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {H : Type v} [AddCommGroup H] [Module R H] {x : H} (hx : x ≠ 0) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, (∀ a ∈ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ^ n, a • x = 0) →
      ∃ y ∈ Submodule.span R {x}, y ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ b ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R, b • y = 0 := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro h
    exact absurd ((one_smul R x).symm.trans (h 1 (by simp))) hx
  | succ n ih =>
    intro h
    by_cases hall : ∀ a ∈ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ^ n, a • x = 0
    · exact ih hall
    · obtain ⟨a, ha, hax⟩ := not_forall₂.mp hall
      refine ⟨a • x, Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self x), hax,
        fun b hb => ?_⟩
      rw [smul_smul]
      exact h (b * a) (by
        rw [pow_succ']
        exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul hb ha)

/-- **Matlis duality detects a map through a submodule of the dual that is dense modulo the
maximal ideal.** Let `R` be local, let `E` be an injective `R`-module with a nonzero element `e`
killed by the maximal ideal, let `H'` be killed elementwise by a power of the maximal ideal and
let `φ : H ⟶ H'`. Let `W` be a submodule of `Hom_R(H', E)` with
`W + 𝔪 · Hom_R(H', E) = Hom_R(H', E)`. If every member of `W` kills `φ`, then `φ = 0`.

This is the sharpening of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.eq_zero_of_forall_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero`
that the **reverse** direction of the local duality step in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0EFX]
needs. There the vanishing of the Ext map gives the vanishing of the maps of the dual that come
from morphisms into the shifted dualizing complex, and those span the dual only modulo the
maximal ideal, the local duality map becoming an isomorphism only after completion. The
statement here is exactly what closes that gap once the span-modulo-`𝔪` is known.

The hypothesis `htor` is `IsIPowerTorsion R H' 𝔪` spelled out, and it holds at every local
cohomology module by the very definition of `Dualizing.derivedPowerTorsionProperty`, whose
objects are those with `𝔪`-power-torsion cohomology; it is spelled out rather than imported so
that this module keeps its light import closure.

*Argument.* Suppose `φ x ≠ 0`. By
`exists_mem_span_ne_zero_maximalIdeal_smul_eq_zero` the submodule `R · φ x` contains a nonzero
`y` killed by `𝔪`; being in `R · φ x`, it is a value of `φ`. Every `ψ` in `W` kills `φ`, so
kills `y`; every `ψ` in `𝔪 · Hom_R(H', E)` kills `y` too, because `𝔪` kills `y`. So every `ψ`
kills `y` by the hypothesis on `W`. But the detection step produces a `ψ` with `ψ y = e ≠ 0`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_forall_mem_comp_eq_zero_of_sup_eq_top {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] {E : Type u} [AddCommGroup E] [Module R E] [Module.Injective R E]
    (e : E) (he : e ≠ 0) (hme : ∀ a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R, a • e = 0)
    {H H' : Type u} [AddCommGroup H] [Module R H] [AddCommGroup H'] [Module R H']
    (htor : ∀ z : H', ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ a ∈ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ^ n, a • z = 0)
    (φ : H →ₗ[R] H') (W : Submodule R (H' →ₗ[R] E))
    (hW : W ⊔ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R • (⊤ : Submodule R (H' →ₗ[R] E)) = ⊤)
    (hφ : ∀ ψ ∈ W, ψ ∘ₗ φ = 0) : φ = 0 := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.zero_apply]
  by_contra hx
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := htor (φ x)
  obtain ⟨y, hyspan, hy0, hym⟩ :=
    exists_mem_span_ne_zero_maximalIdeal_smul_eq_zero (R := R) hx n hn
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.1 hyspan
  -- every map of `H'` into `E` kills `y`
  have hall : ∀ ψ : H' →ₗ[R] E, ψ y = 0 := by
    intro ψ
    have hmem : ψ ∈ W ⊔ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R • (⊤ : Submodule R (H' →ₗ[R] E)) := by
      simp [hW]
    obtain ⟨w, hw, z, hz, hwz⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 hmem
    have hwy : w y = 0 := by
      have h0 : w (φ x) = 0 := LinearMap.congr_fun (hφ w hw) x
      rw [← hc, map_smul, h0, smul_zero]
    have hzy : z y = 0 := by
      refine Submodule.smul_induction_on hz (fun a ha ξ _ => ?_) (fun ξ₁ ξ₂ h₁ h₂ => ?_)
      · change (a • ξ) y = 0
        rw [LinearMap.smul_apply, ← map_smul, hym a ha, map_zero]
      · change (ξ₁ + ξ₂) y = 0
        rw [LinearMap.add_apply, h₁, h₂, add_zero]
    rw [← hwz, LinearMap.add_apply, hwy, hzy, add_zero]
  -- but the detection step produces one that does not
  refine hy0 ?_
  have hzero : LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' y = 0 :=
    eq_zero_of_forall_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero e he hme
      (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R H' y)
      (fun ψ => LinearMap.ext fun r => by
        change ψ (r • y) = 0
        rw [map_smul, hall ψ, smul_zero])
  exact (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply_one R H' y).symm.trans
    (LinearMap.congr_fun hzero 1)

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

